{title: Listen To My Cry}
{artist: Elton Smith and Gilberto Barreto}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 128}

INTRODUCTION
[G] [D] [C] [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bmin] [Amin] [G] [D]

VERSE 1
I [G]cry aloud to [D]You Lord.
I lift [Em]up my voice to [A7]You for mercy.
I [G]pour out my com[D]plaints be[C]fore You. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]
Be[G]fore you I [D]can tell my troubles.
When my [Em]spirit grows [A7]faint within me,
It is [G]You who [D]know my [C]way. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]

CHORUS
Listen [G]to my [A7]cry
for [C]I am in desperate [Am7]need.
[G]Rescue me from [D]those who pur[C]sue me. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]
Listen [G]to my [A7]cry
for [C]I am in desperate [Am7]need.
Then the [G]righteous will [D]gather a[C]bout me. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]

VERSE 2
O [G]Lord, hear my [D]prayer,
[Em]listen to my cry [A7]for mercy;
in your [G]faithfulness and [D]righteousness
[C]come to my relief. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]
Do not [G]bring me into [D]judgment,
for I [Em]am not righteous be[A7]fore you.
I have [G]put my trust in [D]You,
do not [C]hide your face from me. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]

CHORUS
Listen [G]to my [A7]cry
for [C]I am in desperate [Am7]need.
[G]Rescue me from [D]those who pur[C]sue me. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]
Listen [G]to my [A7]cry
for [C]I am in desperate [Am7]need.
Then the [G]righteous will [D]gather a[C]bout me. [Bm] [Am] [C] [Bm] [Am]

